.UE \c
.SS clean\-src
Filter \f[CR]src\f[R] through the \f[CR].gitignore\f[R] it carries
before copying it into the store.
Build artifacts (\f[CR]dist\-newstyle\f[R], \f[CR]result\f[R],
\f[CR].git\f[R]) then do not become part of every derivation that names
the project source.
A rebuild then does not rehash them.
This applies only when \f[CR]src\f[R] is a path.
A derivation is used as\-is.
.PP
\f[I]Type:\f[R] boolean
.PP
\f[I]Default:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
true
.EE
.PP
\f[I]Declared by:\f[R] \- \c
.UR file://%3Cnix-haskell%3E/modules/common
/modules/common
.UE \c
.SS clean\-src\-ignore\-files
The ignore files read when \f[CR]clean\-src\f[R] is enabled.
Paths are relative to the root of the source tree.
.PP
Every pattern uses the root as its base, whichever file it came from.
An anchored pattern in a nested file (\f[CR]dist/*\f[R]) therefore
matches against the root, not against the file\(cqs own directory.
Where that matters, add the pattern to \f[CR]clean\-src\-patterns\f[R]
instead.
.PP
\f[I]Type:\f[R] list of string
.PP
\f[I]Default:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
[
  \(dq/.gitignore\(dq
]
.EE
.PP
\f[I]Example:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
[
  \(dq/.gitignore\(dq
  \(dq/frontend/.gitignore\(dq
]
.EE
.PP
\f[I]Declared by:\f[R] \- \c
.UR file://%3Cnix-haskell%3E/modules/common
/modules/common
.UE \c
