.SS haskell\-nix.project
The built project as haskell.nix returns it: \f[CR]hsPkgs\f[R],
\f[CR]shell\f[R], \f[CR]projectCross\f[R] per cross platform,
\f[CR]plan\-nix\f[R], and the rest.
A replacement value must be a haskell.nix project too: it answers
\f[CR]appendModule\f[R], \f[CR]shell\f[R] and \f[CR]pkg\-set\f[R].
.PP
The shell is haskell.nix\(cqs own, with the common
\f[CR]shell.shellHook\f[R] appended and \f[CR]shell.withHoogle\f[R]
applied.
Both go through \f[CR]overrideAttrs\f[R], so neither is evaluated unless
the shell is.
.PP
With \f[CR]fine\-grained\f[R] on and selecting a package, the project is
re\-evaluated with a module restoring each selected library from its
plan.
The plans read the project as set here, whose components differ from the
final ones only by that restore.
