.SS js\-optimize
\f[B]A function, not a setting.\f[R] A project calls it and uses the
result.
Assign it only to replace what the call does.
.PP
A linked \f[CR].jsexe\f[R] directory with its \f[CR]all.js\f[R]
closure\-compiled.
The rest of the directory is copied unchanged.
It takes the directory, not the package that carries it:
.IP
.EX
js\-optimize {
  platform = \(dqghcjs\(dq;
  package = \(dqfrontend\(dq;
  exe = \(dqfrontend\(dq;
  jsexe = \(dq${frontend}/bin/frontend.jsexe\(dq;
}
.EE
.PP
\f[CR]platform\f[R], \f[CR]package\f[R] and \f[CR]exe\f[R] are only
lookup keys for the settings.
Each can be left out, and an omitted key states nothing.
.PP
Each field of the \f[CR]closure\-compiler\f[R] settings resolves on its
own.
The most specific layer that states a field decides it, in this order:
.IP "1." 3
\f[CR]platforms.<platform>.packages.<package>.components.exes.<exe>.closure\-compiler\f[R]
.IP "2." 3
\f[CR]platforms.<platform>.packages.<package>.closure\-compiler\f[R]
.IP "3." 3
\f[CR]platforms.<platform>.closure\-compiler\f[R]
.IP "4." 3
\f[CR]packages.<package>.components.exes.<exe>.closure\-compiler\f[R],
then \f[CR]packages.<package>.closure\-compiler\f[R]
.IP "5." 3
\f[CR]closure\-compiler\f[R] at the top level, the only layer that holds
every field.
.PP
The settings come from the project\(cqs own values, not a driver\(cqs.
This function runs on a built artifact, outside any driver.
.PP
\f[I]Type:\f[R] function that evaluates to a(n) package
.PP
\f[I]Default:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
<nix\-haskell>/libs/bundle\-optimizer/closure\-compiler/run.nix, run with the settings the named target, package and executable resolve to
.EE
