.SS nixpkgs.cross\-exe
\f[B]A function, not a setting.\f[R] A project calls it and uses the
result.
Assign it only to replace what the call does.
.PP
What this driver builds an executable into, for one cross target.
Both drivers answer to the same name.
The answer carries the executable at \f[CR]bin/<exe>\f[R].
A wasm target\(cqs binary sits at \f[CR]bin/<exe>.wasm\f[R], and a
javascript target\(cqs linked directory at \f[CR]bin/<exe>.jsexe\f[R].
\f[CR]bundles\f[R] optimizes this result.
.PP
This driver builds one derivation per package, so the executable\(cqs
own name does not affect the lookup.
The function takes it only to keep the one interface both drivers answer
to.
