\f[I]Declared by:\f[R] \- \c
.UR file://%3Cnix-haskell%3E/modules/nixpkgs
/modules/nixpkgs
.UE \c
.SS nixpkgs.pkgsCross
Cross package sets for \f[CR]project.projectCross\f[R], keyed by
\f[CR]pkgs.pkgsCross\f[R] platform name.
An entry replaces the package set the driver would otherwise take from
\f[CR]pkgs.pkgsCross\f[R].
A compiler bringing its own toolchain needs the replacement, since that
toolchain has to become the whole set\(cqs.
.PP
\f[I]Type:\f[R] attribute set of raw value
.PP
\f[I]Default:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
<nix\-haskell>/libs/nixpkgs/cross\-pkgs.nix
.EE
.PP
for every \f[CR]compiler.platforms\f[R] entry carrying a
\f[CR]toolchain\f[R]: a package set for that platform whose whole
toolchain is the compiler\(cqs own, built non\-static so a build can use
the compiler\(cqs shared libraries.
A platform without an entry gets none, and the driver falls back to
\f[CR]pkgs.pkgsCross.<platform>\f[R].
.PP
\f[I]Example:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
{ wasi32 = my\-wasi\-pkgs; }
.EE
.PP
