.SS platforms
Per\-platform customization, keyed by \f[CR]pkgs.pkgsCross\f[R] platform
name (the keys of \f[CR]shell.crossPlatforms\f[R] and
\f[CR]projectCross\f[R]).
.PP
A cabal file or project file can make a package\(cqs flags, and through
them its dependencies, conditional on the platform.
Each driver handles that differently:
.IP \(bu 2
haskell.nix follows those conditionals through its solver
.IP \(bu 2
nixpkgs has no solver, so state here what the conditionals would have
decided
.PP
The flags reach the point where a package\(cqs dependencies are
computed, not only its configuration.
.PP
\f[CR]wasm\-opt\f[R] and \f[CR]closure\-compiler\f[R] are the bundle
optimizer settings for whatever is built for this target.
The \f[CR]packages\f[R] entries under them narrow a setting to one
package, and their \f[CR]components.exes\f[R] entries to one executable
of it.
