.SS wasm\-jsffi
\f[B]A function, not a setting.\f[R] A project calls it and uses the
result.
Assign it only to replace what the call does.
.PP
The \f[CR]ghc_wasm_jsffi.js\f[R] without which a GHC\-built wasm module
cannot be instantiated, read out of the binary by the compiler that
built it:
.IP
.EX
wasm\-jsffi {
  ghc = config.<driver>.cross\-compiler \(dqwasi32\(dq;
  wasm = \(dq${frontend}/bin/frontend.wasm\(dq;
}
.EE
.PP
The compiler must be the one that produced the binary, and
\f[CR]<driver>.cross\-compiler\f[R] names that compiler.
Run this on the binary as linked, before \f[CR]wasm\-optimize\f[R]
strips the sections it reads.
.PP
\f[I]Type:\f[R] function that evaluates to a(n) package
.PP
\f[I]Default:\f[R]
.IP
.EX
<nix\-haskell>/libs/cross/wasm\-jsffi.nix
.EE
